  "mathematical_review": {
    "passed": true,
    "checks": [
      {
        "id": "abelianity_iff_normal_form",
        "passed": true,
        "evidence": "Tag 014S makes K(A) triangulated, hence pre-triangulated. Tag 05QU identifies kernels, cokernels, and the projection-coprojection normal form. With Tag 0109, the normal form gives kernels and cokernels and makes the canonical coimage-to-image map the identity on the middle summand; conversely abelianness supplies kernels for every morphism."
      },
      {
        "id": "normal_form_implies_split_short_exact_sequences",
        "passed": true,
        "evidence": "For a monomorphism a between degree-zero complexes, the normal form supplies b with aba=a. Homotopies between such maps vanish, so this equality holds in A; monicity gives ba=1, which splits the short exact sequence."
      },
      {
        "id": "split_complex_decomposition_and_contracting_homotopy",
        "passed": true,
        "evidence": "Splitting 0->Z^n->X^n->B^(n+1)->0 and 0->B^n->Z^n->H^n->0 yields X^n=B^n+H^n+B^(n+1) with d(b,h,c)=(c,0,0). For C^n=B^n+B^(n+1), s^n(b,c)=(0,b) satisfies d^(n-1)s^n+s^(n+1)d^n=1 with the displayed degrees and signs."
      },
      {
        "id": "cohomology_functor_full_faithful_essentially_surjective",
        "passed": true,
        "evidence": "Tag 0116 makes H* well-defined on K(A). The chosen inclusion/projection maps are inverse in K(A) and induce identity on cohomology; u maps to i_Y u p_X and every f equals i_Y H*(f) p_X. Thus H* is fully faithful, and H*H*=H* plus X isomorphic to H*(X) gives essential surjectivity."
      },
      {
        "id": "graded_category_conclusion",
        "passed": true,
        "evidence": "For zero-differential complexes the homotopy relation is equality, so the full subcategory is Gr(A). Tags 0125 and 0126 identify it and prove it abelian. The equivalence therefore makes K(A) abelian. The payload correctly records that the splittings are noncanonical and asserts no natural isomorphism H*=>Id."
      }
    ]
  },
